From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom-smbchg: don't let a battery overvoltage stop charging

CHGR_CFG2 bit 4 (CHG_BAT_OV_ECC) makes a battery overvoltage disable
charging. The driver leaves it as it finds it, and on a Redmi 4 Prime
(PMI8950, msm8953-xiaomi-markw) it is set (CHGR_CFG2 0x51). The battery
overvoltage comparator (BAT_IF RT_STS bit 4) trips at the top of every
charge: at 4.35-4.37 V with a 4.38 V float, at about 4.30 V with a
4.35 V float, right after termination. Each time chg-error latched and
charging stayed stopped until the charge path restarted, so the battery
sat at about 90 %.

Qualcomm's downstream qpnp-smbcharger clears this bit at init on
PMI8950, PMI8937 and PMI8940, as on PMI8994. It also restarts charging
if an overvoltage is already latched (SMBCHG_BATT_OV_WA,
batt_ov_wa_check()). Do the same.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/of_irq.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/cleanup.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
@@ -1466,6 +1467,7 @@
  */
 static int smbchg_init(struct smbchg_chip *chip)
 {
+	unsigned int value;
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
@@ -1498,12 +1500,30 @@
 	ret = qcom_pmic_sec_masked_write(
 		chip->regmap, chip->base + SMBCHG_CHGR_CHGR_CFG2,
 		CHARGER_INHIBIT_BIT | AUTO_RECHG_BIT | I_TERM_BIT |
-			P2F_CHG_TRAN_BIT | CHG_EN_SRC_BIT,
+			CHG_BAT_OV_ECC_BIT | P2F_CHG_TRAN_BIT | CHG_EN_SRC_BIT,
 		CHG_INHIBIT_EN | AUTO_RCHG_EN | CURRENT_TERM_EN |
 			PRE_FAST_AUTO | CHG_EN_SRC_CMD);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The configuration above also clears CHG_BAT_OV_ECC, so that a
+	 * battery overvoltage no longer stops charging. With it set, the
+	 * charger stopped at the top of every charge and stayed stopped. If
+	 * an overvoltage has already stopped it, restart charging: disable
+	 * it here, and the enable below turns it back on.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_read(chip->regmap, chip->base + SMBCHG_BAT_IF_RT_STS,
+			  &value);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	if (value & BAT_OV_BIT) {
+		ret = smbchg_charging_enable(chip, false);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		msleep(200);
+	}
+
 	/* Set recharge threshold to 100mV */
 	ret = qcom_pmic_sec_masked_write(chip->regmap,
 					 chip->base + SMBCHG_CHGR_CFG,
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.h
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.h
@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@
 #define CHARGER_INHIBIT_BIT		BIT(0)
 #define AUTO_RECHG_BIT			BIT(2)
 #define I_TERM_BIT			BIT(3)
+#define CHG_BAT_OV_ECC_BIT		BIT(4)
 #define P2F_CHG_TRAN_BIT		BIT(5)
 #define CHG_EN_POLARITY_BIT		BIT(6)
 #define CHG_EN_SRC_BIT			BIT(7)
